I'd like to talk about an important text message I received from my close
friend, Tuan.

He sent it to me about a year ago after finishing his studies abroad. The message was short and simple. He wrote, "I'm finally coming back! I can't wait to see you again. I've missed you so much!"

He sent me that message because he wanted to let me know that he had booked his flight and would be back in Vietnam in just a few days. We've known each other since primary school, so we're very close. Although we kept in touch through social media and video calls, it wasn't the same as meeting in person.

When I read the message, I felt really excited because I had been looking forward to seeing him for such a long time. We immediately started making plans to meet, have dinner together, and catch up on everything that had happened over the past year.

This message was important to me because it reminded me how valuable true friendship is. No matter how far apart we were, we always stayed connected. His return meant that we could finally spend time together again instead of just chatting online. Even now, I still remember how happy I felt when I received that message.
